  "id": "thewash",
  "neon": "#7fe3ff",
  "note": "THE WASH — the launderette on the west side of Ironside Street, and the lowest thing on it.\n\nThe tile's prose: a single-storey shopfront that is almost entirely window, blue-white light hard\nenough to lay a rectangle over the kerb, THE WASH in cold tube neon over the door, and somebody on\nthe bench inside doing nothing in particular.\n\nThe shed stays low. What puts it on the skyline is the flue, which is also where the steam goes,\nand the lantern over the machines, which is how a one-room shed full of dryers gets daylight. The\nlantern is glazed on three sides and lit at night, so from up the street the building is a low\nbright box with a second, smaller bright box on top of it.\n\nThe glazing is one band in four bays between slim white piers, over a tiled stall riser, with the\ndoor at the north end. The fascia above it is a separate white band standing proud of the wall,\nand the name is on it in the `tube` hand. The south flank is blank, so the trade word is painted\non it large; it is a second sign, so it says `$trade` and not the name. The north flank keeps its\nrow of dryer vents.",
  "pal": "ty_trm_wash",
